.TH LYRICSYNC 1 "August 2026" "lyricsync" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lyricsync \- generate synchronized LRC lyrics from audio and plain text lyrics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lyricsync
.RB ( \-\-input-song
.IR song " | " \-\-input-vocals
.IR vocals )
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lyricsync
aligns a plain-text lyrics file to an audio track and writes synchronized LRC
lyrics.
It can either extract vocals from an original song before alignment, or skip
vocal extraction when an existing vocals file is supplied.
.P
Exactly one of
.B \-\-input-song
or
.B \-\-input-vocals
is required.
If
.B \-\-input-lyrics
is omitted,
.B lyricsync
derives it from the input path by removing the final extension and appending
.IR .txt .
If
.B \-\-output-lrc
is omitted,
.B lyricsync
derives it from the input path by removing the final extension and appending
.IR .lrc .
A defaulted LRC output path is rejected when the file already exists.
.SH TASK OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-input-song " PATH"
Original song to process. Vocals are extracted before lyrics alignment.
.TP
.BI \-\-input-vocals " PATH"
Already extracted vocals to use. This skips vocal extraction.
.TP
.BI \-\-output-vocals " PATH"
Save extracted vocals at
.IR PATH .
When
.B \-\-input-vocals
is used, this option is ignored with a warning.
.TP
.BI \-\-input-lyrics " PATH"
Plain-text lyrics to align.
.TP
.BI \-\-output-lrc " PATH"
Synced lyrics output path.
.TP
.BI \-l " PATH" ", " \-\-lyrics " PATH"
Alias for
.BR \-\-input-lyrics .
.TP
.BI \-o " PATH" ", " \-\-output " PATH"
Alias for
.BR \-\-output-lrc .
.TP
.BI \-\-vocals-output " PATH"
Alias for
.BR \-\-output-vocals .
.SH MODEL OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-model-vocal " PATH"
MDX-Net ONNX model used for vocal extraction.
.TP
.BI \-\-model-ctc " PATH"
CTC ONNX model used for lyrics alignment.
.TP
.BI \-\-tokenizer " PATH"
CTC tokenizer tokens file.
.TP
.BI \-\-onnx-provider " KIND"
ONNX Runtime execution provider.
.I KIND
must be one of
.BR auto ,
.BR cpu ,
or
.BR cuda .
The default is
.BR auto .
.TP
.BI \-\-onnx-device " N"
CUDA device id. The default is
.BR 0 .
.SH AUDIO OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-ffmpeg " PATH"
FFmpeg executable. The default is
.BR ffmpeg .
.TP
.BI \-\-temp-dir " PATH"
Directory used for temporary files. The default is
.BR /tmp .
.TP
.BI \-\-vocals-format " KIND"
Extracted vocals container format.
.I KIND
must be one of
.BR wav ,
.BR flac ,
.BR mp3 ,
or
.BR opus .
The default is inferred from
.B \-\-output-vocals
when possible, otherwise
.BR wav .
.TP
.BI \-\-format " KIND"
Alias for
.BR \-\-vocals-format .
.TP
.BI \-\-chunk-seconds " N"
MDX chunk size in seconds. The default is
.BR 30 .
.TP
.BI \-\-margin-seconds " N"
MDX chunk margin in seconds. The default is
.BR 3 .
.TP
.BI \-\-compensate " X"
Output gain. The default is
.BR 1.035 .
.TP
.BI \-\-n-fft " N"
STFT size. The default is
.BR 6144 .
.TP
.BI \-\-hop " N"
STFT hop size. The default is
.BR 1024 .
.TP
.BI \-\-dim-f " N"
Override model frequency bins.
.TP
.BI \-\-dim-t " N"
Override model time frames.
.TP
.BI \-\-model-output " KIND"
Model output stem.
.I KIND
must be
.B vocals
or
.BR instrumental .
The default is
.BR vocals .
.TP
.BI \-\-clip-mode " KIND"
Final clipping policy.
.I KIND
must be
.B clamp
or
.BR none .
The default is
.BR clamp .
.TP
.B \-\-denoise
Run denoising inference mode.
.SH LYRICS OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-ctc-debug-dump " PATH"
Write a CTC parity debug dump to
.IR PATH .
.TP
.BI \-\-split-size " KIND"
Lyrics split size.
.I KIND
must be one of
.BR current ,
.BR word ,
.BR char ,
or
.BR sentence .
The default is
.BR word .
.TP
.BI \-\-star-frequency " KIND"
Star-token placement.
.I KIND
must be one of
.BR none ,
.BR edges ,
or
.BR segment .
The default is
.BR edges .
.TP
.BI \-\-romanization " KIND"
Romanization backend.
.I KIND
must be
.B off
or
.BR icu .
The default is
.BR icu .
.TP
.BI \-\-language " CODE"
Three-letter language code used by lyrics preprocessing. The default is
.BR eng .
.TP
.BI \-\-emissions " KIND"
Model emission values.
.I KIND
must be one of
.BR log-probabilities ,
.BR logits ,
or
.BR probabilities .
The default is
.BR logits .
.TP
.B \-\-keep-temp-files
Keep generated temporary files.
.TP
.B \-\-romanize
Select ICU romanization. This is equivalent to
.BR "\-\-romanization icu" .
.SH GENERAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage information and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LRC_VOCALS_MODEL
Default vocal extraction model path.
.TP
.B LRC_CTC_MODEL
Default CTC alignment model path.
.TP
.B LRC_CTC_TOKENIZER
Default CTC tokenizer path.
.TP
.B LRC_ONNX_PROVIDER
Default ONNX provider, unless
.B \-\-onnx-provider
is passed.
.TP
.B LRC_ONNX_DEVICE
Default ONNX CUDA device id, unless
.B \-\-onnx-device
is passed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I models/UVR-MDX-NET-Voc_FT.onnx
Development-tree default vocal extraction model.
.TP
.I models/mms-onnx/onnx/model.onnx
Development-tree default CTC alignment model.
.TP
.I models/mms-onnx/tokens.txt
Development-tree default CTC tokenizer.
.TP
.I /usr/share/lyricsync/models
System model directory fallback.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/lyricsync/models
Local system model directory fallback.
.SH EXAMPLES
.P
Extract vocals from a song and generate synced lyrics:
.P
.EX
lyricsync --input-song song.mp3 \e
    --input-lyrics full_lyrics.txt \e
    --output-vocals vocals.opus \e
    --output-lrc synced_lyrics.lrc
.EE
.P
Generate synced lyrics from already extracted vocals:
.P
.EX
lyricsync --input-vocals vocals.opus \e
    --input-lyrics full_lyrics.txt \e
    --output-lrc synced_lyrics.lrc
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1)
